1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,528
Narrator: Scenario 69. Monitoring, performance, and reliability.

2
00:00:07,128 --> 00:00:16,560
B: All synthetic checks are green, but one customer says file uploads keep failing. Could this be a problem with their network or browser?

3
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:26,976
A: That is possible, but our checks may not cover the affected account type, region, or upload path. We should examine their examples first.

4
00:00:27,576 --> 00:00:39,720
C: They supplied three failing request identifiers and UTC timestamps. The requests came from an enterprise account using large files through the regional gateway.

5
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:50,064
B: Our probe uploads a small file through the global endpoint. It does not exercise that regional gateway or the larger enterprise upload limit.

6
00:00:50,664 --> 00:01:01,056
A: Then the green result has limited relevance to this complaint. Let us trace those requests and compare gateway responses with the upload service logs.

7
00:01:01,656 --> 00:01:13,200
C: The gateway returns a timeout after thirty seconds. The upload service continues processing, so a customer retry might create another copy of the file.

8
00:01:13,800 --> 00:01:26,040
A: Please check whether the request identifier prevents duplicate processing before recommending retries. We also need to confirm completed uploads remain accessible to the customer.

9
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:36,864
B: Can we reproduce the timeout safely with a test enterprise account? I would prefer direct evidence before changing the gateway limit for all customers.

10
00:01:37,464 --> 00:01:49,824
A: Yes. Use a non-sensitive test file in the same region and record size, duration, and response codes. Any configuration change still needs normal approval.

11
00:01:50,424 --> 00:02:00,432
C: I will update the customer now with confirmed findings and avoid assigning blame. When should I promise the next progress update from our team?

12
00:02:01,032 --> 00:02:12,048
A: Give them 16:30 UTC as the next update time, not a recovery estimate. I will own reproduction, and the service owner will assess mitigation.

13
00:02:12,648 --> 00:02:24,360
B: Agreed. We will add representative regional upload coverage after validating the failure, and keep the customer case open until they confirm the workflow succeeds.
